        "Type": "print",
        "Language": "Japanese",
        "Subject": "Tourism",
        "Publisher Note": "\"Revised and corrected edition. Comprised of seven sightseeing routes through 1890s Tokyo, the top half of each leaf is an engraved map of sightseeing areas such as temples, gardens, banks, theaters, bridges, an amusement park, and a foreigner’s quarter. Notes on the bottom half. The final three leaves contain useful references such as the ideal places to visit every month for flower viewing.\" (Ursus Books, 2024)",
